# Data API grants

From 30 October 2026, new objects in `public` are not reachable by supabase-js, PostgREST, or GraphQL until granted. Existing objects keep their current grants. Do not backfill them and do not change default privileges.

In the same migration that creates the object, grant only the roles and privileges that callers need. RLS still limits rows. `anon` gets nothing unless the object is intentionally public. `postgres` gets nothing unless a cron job or definer function in the same migration calls it.

| Caller | Typical grant |
|---|---|
| Admin API routes (service role via supabase-js) | `select, insert, update, delete` to `service_role` |
| Signed-in mobile or web client | Only the verbs its RLS policies allow, to `authenticated` |
| RPC | `execute` on the function to the roles that call it |
| Inserts into an identity or serial column via the API | `usage, select` on that sequence to the same roles |

```sql
grant select, insert, update, delete on public.your_table to service_role;
grant select on public.your_table to authenticated;
```
